<article class="env-corollary" id="04HB">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HB">Corollary <span data-tag="04HB">3.5.1.32</span>.</a> Let $n$ be a nonnegative integer. Then a simplicial set $X$ is $n$-connective if and only if it is nonempty and the diagonal map $\delta _{X}: X \rightarrow X \times X$ is $(n-1)$-connective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a data-tag="00UW" href="/tag/00UW">3.1.8.2</a> and Proposition <a data-tag="02L2" href="/tag/02L2">3.1.7.23</a>, we can reduce to the situation where $X$ is a Kan complex. In this case, the follows by applying Corollary <a data-tag="04HL" href="/tag/04HL">3.5.1.31</a> in the special case $Y = \Delta ^0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
